    "kind": "good",
    "note": "The carbon to carbon bond forming step, and the reason the enolate is drawn with its charge on oxygen: the nucleophilic atom is the alpha CARBON, so step 1 needs three arrows and not one. The oxygen lone pair pushes back into the C to O bond, the C to C pi pair makes the new bond to the aldehyde, and the aldehyde pi pair goes onto its own oxygen. Drawing only the middle arrow leaves the enolate oxygen with a charge it no longer has any reason to carry and the alpha carbon with five bonds. The enolate itself is made in good-enolate-formation-from-acetone-by-hydroxide and the condensation that follows is good-e1cb-elimination-of-a-beta-hydroxy-ketone-to-an-enone."
